#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:5
#: 8d412563a12b48d8b897da4502215e7d
msgid "BLHeli32,AM32, and BLHeli_S ESCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:7
#: 1c5da1929c1b4bd2995fbd340103a784
msgid "if you are using BLHeli32 ESCs, be sure to update to the latest BLHeliSuite32 Rev32.10.0.0 firmware, to avoid surprise uncontrollable motor starts due to a BLHel32 firmware bug!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:9
#: 4ecdb87b9b7a4d9e8f29441e903182d4
msgid "The BLHeli firmware and configuration applications were developed to allow the configuration of ESCs and provide additional features. ESCs with this firmware allow configuring timing, motor direction, LEDs, motor drive frequency, etc.  Before attempting to use BLHeli please follow the :ref:`DShot setup instructions <common-dshot-escs>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:11
#: e97f6d93695846ed8528ba3e93071cc4
msgid "Depending on the ESC, BLHeli/BLHeli_S/BLHeli32/AM32 provides the following features:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:13
#: 70caa9248bca4799b98e7d149dbbf281
msgid "Pass-Through support in ArduPilot allows the BLHeliSuite, AM32 and other ESC configurators to be used to configure the ESCs while remaining connected to the autopilot via USB cable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:14
#: c1c377a9258446ea98fd5426341a8518
msgid ":ref:`Reversible DShot <blheli32-reversible-dshot>` (aka 3D mode) allows the motor to be spun in either direction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:15
#: 1fde70d56f3c44ca9230e9b6ae7aea89
msgid ":ref:`Bi-directional DShot <bidir-dshot>` allows the ESCs to send RPM back to the autopilot without the need for an additional telemetry connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:16
#: d27059b1cde84c4e9926c794d8ec8f9a
msgid ":ref:`ESC Telemetry <blheli32-esc-telemetry>` allows the ESCs to send RPM, voltage and current information back to the autopilot so that it can be logged, viewed in real-time or even allow the removal of a :ref:`battery monitor <esc-telemetry-based-battery-monitor>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:18
#: 30b5427ef951420495f58f30578b18d4
msgid "\"BLHeli\" (and now AM32) covers multiple (sometimes competing) projects providing ESCs firmware and accompanying configuration software"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:20
#: a73b9df8311f4759aeacbd4c3200ce77
msgid "BLHeli was the original open source software that is no longer maintained and is not available on modern ESCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:21
#: 7ceb551a48644cab8646a9ccd8d074b4
msgid "BLHeli32is closed source and based on 32bit ARM MCUs and development and licensing was terminated in 2024.  All modern BLHeli ESCs use BLHeli32 but will be replaced with AM32 in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:22
#: 4fdb5991db94484684bea00aee53b281
msgid "`AM32 <https://am32.ca>`__ is open source with the same features as BLHeli32 before it became unavailable for new designs but continues to evolve."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:23
#: 85f79747e830452288f24a1e02e891b3
msgid "`BLHeli_S <https://github.com/bitdump/BLHeli>`__ is open source and 16bit.  This is no longer actively maintained but the last published version, 16.7, is installed by default on \"BLHeli_S\" ESCs when shipped from the factory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:24
#: 9a463fb7f736428eb2c80b9c05770d63
msgid "`BLHeli_S JESC <https://jflight.net>`__ is paid, closed source software and 16bit allowing it to run on lower end hardware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:25
#: bd20356a75dd4cd4b326f32127620e62
msgid "`BLHeli_S BlueJay <https://github.com/mathiasvr/bluejay>`__ is free, open source software and 16bit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:26
#: 57f61c8bd2ba4a8a8309b6b49f26fe2f
msgid "`Web-based ESC Configurator for the above <https://esc-configurator.com/>`__  (due to timing variations, being internet based, reliability of connection thru ArduPilot is variable)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:28
#: a1f6dd0775104aef9ad28ef414915893
msgid "firmware 4.5 or later required to use this ESC Configurator tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:31
#: f90848523f3c44278ce93e250a3983fd
msgid "Pass-Through Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:34
#: f213f22208c0407e97cebf10ed4ebc3f
msgid "This feature is only available on NON IOMCU outputs. Autopilots which have an IOMCU co-processsor (usually marked as having \"MAIN\" outputs from the IOMCU and \"AUX\" outputs from the main cpu) will not pass-through on those outputs. Use this feature on \"AUX\" or \"FMU\" outputs with DShot capability. For Plane, Rover and Sub, be mindful that using AUX outputs for vehicle-critical controls removes the benefits of an IOMCU. For Copter, IOMCU redundancy is not effective since it has no \"MANUAL\" control mode. For maximum robustness (on Plane which has a manual mode which can be used if the FMU fails), switch your motors to \"AUX\" or \"FMU\" only when configuring with passthrough, and move them back to \"MAIN\" once configuration is complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:38
#: 7586808d6e8447eda8e1e67477d1b0e2
msgid "The Pass-Through feature allows BLHeli32, AM32, and BLHeli_S ESCs to be upgraded and configured using the corresponding BLHeliSuite32, AM32 Configurator, or BLHeliSuite application (running on the user's PC) while the ESCs remain connected to the autopilot.  To use this feature please follow these steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:40
#: ded1a63e2f54472ebe82518be3297c56
msgid "Download and install `Linux or Windows AM32 configurator <https://am32.ca/downloads>`__ (for use with AM32 ESCs), `BLHeliSuite32 <https://github.com/bitdump/BLHeli/releases>`__ (for use with BLHeli32/AM32 ESCs), `BLHeliSuite <https://github.com/bitdump/BLHeli>`__ (for BLHeli_S ESC) or `JESC configurator <https://github.com/jflight-public/jesc-configurator/releases>`__ (for use with BLHeli_S JESC) on your PC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:41
#: 12aabb73b16f494f84af5cf625584749
msgid "Connect your PC to the autopilot using a USB cable and then connect with a ground station (e.g. Mission Planner, QGC)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:42
#: 8d3c163e843441488740e4eb18eafbe2
msgid "Disconnect your propellers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:43
#: 63baf0199521494fac02fb99ab4c0591
msgid "Set :ref:`SERVO_BLH_AUTO <SERVO_BLH_AUTO>` to 1 to automatically enable pass-through on all outputs configured as motors (e.g. :ref:`SERVOx_FUNCTION <SERVO9_FUNCTION>` = \"Motor1\", \"Motor2\", etc) for multicopters and quadplanes or throttle (e.g. those with :ref:`SERVOx_FUNCTION <SERVO9_FUNCTION>` set to 70 (\"throttle\"), 73 (\"throttle left\") or 74 (\"throttle right\")) on rovers.  For most multicopters, quadplanes and rovers this will do the right thing but for planes, set :ref:`SERVO_BLH_MASK <SERVO_BLH_MASK>` to enable pass-through on the appropriate servo outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:44
#: eb10732826fd490bb9ffb5184af974ec
msgid "If your PC is connected to the autopilot using a telemetry radio (instead of using USB cable as recommended above) set :ref:`SERVO_BLH_PORT <SERVO_BLH_PORT>` to the autopilot port connected to the telemetry radio.  Beware that this is does NOT specify the port used for :ref:`ESC telemetry <blheli32-esc-telemetry>` feedback to your autopilot!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:45
#: 5b715a240177405e9315a9634b477f88
msgid "Plug in the vehicle's battery to power the ESC's"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:46
#: 1d9702b6492c4470a00297c0e5ce871d
msgid "If using a safety switch ensure it is pushed (or disabled by setting :ref:`BRD_SAFETY_DEFLT <BRD_SAFETY_DEFLT>` = 0).  (``BRD_SAFETYENABLE`` in older firmware versions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:47
#: e9b09ad4889d43f88a51be7458e722a5
msgid "Disconnect the ground station (but leave the USB cable connected)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:48
#: d02e5313c421447f9f1ef06ce9a7db95
msgid "Start the ESC configuration software and connect to the autopilot's COM port by selecting \"BLHeli32/AM32 Bootloader (Betaflight/Cleanflight)\" from the interfaces menu.  Press \"Connect\" and \"Read Setup\".  You should be able to upgrade and configure all connected ESCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:55
#: 404f0a3634c34863a599f904fc508784
msgid "ArduPilot firmware supports the pass-through protocol with up-to-date BLHeli32, AM32 firmware and BLHeliSuite32, or BLHeli_S firmware and BLHeliSuite only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blheli32-passthru.rst:58
#: a886375c2f284352823f9f5a5b4a0080
msgid "For pass-through to function, the autopilot must be configured to use one of the DShot protocols.  If you wish to eventually use one of the other protocols (e.g. PWM, OneShot125) that the ESC supports, you may still configure the ESCs using Pass-Through (e.g. change motor directions, set min/max values, etc) but then finally re-configure the autopilot to *not* use DShot.  Once the autopilot and ESCs are rebooted the ESC should auto-detect that the ESCs are no longer using DShot."
msgstr ""
